<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 3.1 Exercises</heading>
    <paragraph>In using the technique of integration by parts, you must carefully choose which expression is u. For each of the following problems, use the guidelines in this section to choose u. Do not evaluate the integrals.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{x^{3}e^{2x}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$u = x 3 u = x 3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{x^{3}\ln (x)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="3" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{y^{3}\cos ydy}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$u = y 3 u = y 3$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="4" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{x^{2}\arctan x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{e^{3x}\sin (2x)dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$u = sin ( 2 x ) u = sin ( 2 x )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Find the integral by using the simplest method. Not all problems require integration by parts.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="6" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{v\sin vdv}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="7" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\ln x dx}$$ (Hint: $$\int{\ln x dx}$$ is equivalent to $${\int{1 \cdot \ln (x)dx}}.)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- x + x ln x + C - x + x ln x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="8" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{x\cos x dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
